Short:        Codes from Mare/Zenon
Author:       mluukkai@rieska.oulu.fi
Uploader:     mluukkai rieska oulu fi
Type:         dev/asm
Architecture: m68k-amigaos

 Included  are full sourcecodes to demo NoSeX! by zenon in this packet. It
was 2nd at the abduction 98 party held in Oulu/Finnland.  Yes
you really can compile and run it and Yes it includes my last
assembler 3d-engine too. Also there are some other assembly-coded demo
routines in this packet. (raycasting tunnel, angle/distance tunnel etc)

 All these routines DON'T have c2p-routine included as I don't have one
which I'm allowed to spread.  But don't worry you can use some publicly
available c2ps to make routines work.

 All routines are in assembly language and are optimized to be quite fast on
060-based amigas.  About other 68k processors I don't care.

 These routines were released due to the fact that I moved to
c++/java/delphi-coding and sold my amiga.

 I don't mind if You use these codes in your demo,game or anything, but
please e-mail me incase you do ;)  Module prototyyppi and pictures by
tohe are not for public use.  

 These routines should work well and not destroy or otherwise mess your
computer upp.  But if something like that should happen, I don't take any
responsibility.

 If some problems occur with these sources then e-mail me at:
mluukkai@rieska.oulu.fi.  Please don't ask me for the c2p-routine as I can't
give it to you.


 
